Mechanisms / acceptance pointers
crates/bbt-mux/src/ring.rs:614 — seal_hot commits and preserves the complete CRC-framed segment in content-addressed blobs, then publishes the new hot boundary and linked descriptor head before retiring files. No checkpoint is required to rotate.
crates/bbt-mux/src/ring.rs:666 — one-segment hydration cache; content digest, length, identity, framing, CRC and sequence validation reuse the hot reader. Committed descriptor chains define the retained prefix.
crates/bbt-mux/src/ring.rs:700 — checkpoints can cover an earlier retained cold cursor; newest two blob references survive hot rotation.
crates/bbt-mux/src/ring.rs:795 — 64 KiB / 20 ms output group commit; control, checkpoint, sealing and supervisor shutdown flush. captured_sequence and committed_sequence are distinct. Data sync precedes the marker; capture-owner death may discard an uncommitted group.
crates/bbt-mux/src/ring.rs:955 — bounded history pages span sealed segments and hot records; no fabricated rollover gap; genuine unavailable prefixes retain the explicit gap contract.
crates/bbt-mux/src/supervisor.rs:1124 — full/detached logic notifications no longer gate ring-backed PTY reads. One latest notification remains; the legacy ring-less primitive retains its earlier queue backpressure.
crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:516 — startup replays through the captured cursor; intermediate historical checkpoints coalesce to the recovered tail.
crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:701 — verified-generation sequence jumps hydrate omitted records before applying the latest live event, without replaying terminal effects.
crates/bbt-mux/tests/logic.rs:561 — stop logic, attach an unread notification queue, write 20 MiB, verify completion/latency BEFORE restart, restore the red tail without a gap, compare every raw byte by SHA-256, and retain the same child PID.
crates/bbt-mux/tests/logic.rs:753 — stall a live receiver while 5 MiB flows; coalesced notifications recover to the tail with no gap.
crates/bbt-mux/tests/ring.rs:130 — complete but uncommitted records are visible as captured, not durable; reopening rejects the suffix and explicitly reports the missing range; flush makes the retry durable.
crates/bbt-mux/tests/ring.rs:161 — corrupt sealed payload cannot masquerade as complete history/replay.
crates/bbt-mux/tests/ring.rs:190 — hot rollover, cold history, two reachable checkpoints and reopen/replay round-trip.

