Limits / deliberately untouched
No total cold-byte quota is introduced (never-delete). A future quota must stop capture with a durable explicit gap and continue draining the PTY; it cannot pause the agent. Cold descriptor metadata grows with retained history; only one decoded segment is cached.
Real disk-full/media faults, strict power-cut ordering/F_FULLFSYNC, multi-minute/1000-seat sustained throughput, supervisor-death process survival, Linux and macOS 14 were not tested. Uncommitted group loss on capture-owner death is explicit; logic restart while that supervisor lives retains captured data.
Pre-W1.2b orphan archives without committed descriptor chains remain outside the guaranteed prefix. Logical row metadata can be unavailable outside loaded checkpoint/segment indexes; raw history remains readable.
No new runtime, dependencies, Cargo.lock change, GUI/render changes, adapter work, user configuration or secrets. Shared peer changes remain untouched. Own signed commit and scope/signature checks are reported in the ICQ handoff rather than self-referencing this log.
